,"kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the student should ideally be able to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Understand major food-processing technologies."},{"text":"Understand food manufacturing equipment."},{"text":"Map complete production processes."},{"text":"Calculate basic process yields."},{"text":"Understand HACCP principles."},{"text":"Understand GMP and food-safety systems."},{"text":"Perform basic production planning."},{"text":"Calculate and interpret OEE."},{"text":"Conduct basic root-cause analysis."},{"text":"Apply Lean manufacturing techniques."},{"text":"Understand preventive and predictive maintenance."},{"text":"Understand inventory and supply-chain principles."},{"text":"Use Excel for production analysis."},{"text":"Build Power BI manufacturing dashboards."},{"text":"Understand ERP/MRP workflows."},{"text":"Understand basic PLC/SCADA/MES concepts."},{"text":"Complete 2–3 food manufacturing projects."},{"text":"Complete an internship involving actual plant-floor operations."}]}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The strongest profile for a future Plant Manager (Food) is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Food Processing","Food Safety","Production Management","Lean Manufacturing","Quality","Supply Chain","Digital Manufacturing"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The student should not aim to become only a food technologist. A Plant Manager needs to understand the entire manufacturing system—people, machines, materials, quality, safety, cost, production, and technology."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended pathway"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Tech Food Processing Technology","Food Manufacturing + Food Safety","Production / Process Engineering Internship","Production / Process Engineer","Senior Production Engineer","Assistant Production Manager","Production Manager","Plant Manager","Senior Plant Manager","Manufacturing Head / Operations Director"]},{"type":"flow","items":["Food Processin